# 9. Video Duration Tracking

Clearly distinguish:

- Planned duration.
- Actual watched duration.

For example, a video may have a planned duration of 60 minutes and actual watched progress of 20 minutes.

Use an appropriate numeric progress-log mechanism to record actual watched minutes.

Do not treat `isCompleted = true` as equivalent to recording actual watched duration.

A video may be completed after its actual watched duration reaches or exceeds its planned duration, but completion rules must remain explicit and validated.

Avoid adding a separate video-specific database table.

