# 11. Date and Time Handling

Reuse the existing Daywell Ethiopian/Gregorian calendar and date utilities.

Do not introduce a second date system.

Requirements:

- Date-only values use the existing canonical date representation.
- Timestamps remain distinct from date-only values.
- Do not derive a user's intended calendar date by accidentally converting through UTC.
- Ethiopian/Gregorian conversion remains centralized in existing utilities.
- Daily progress calculations use the stored canonical date.
- Schedule calculations use the existing date conventions.

The BIM outreach daily totals must be correct regardless of whether the user views dates in Ethiopian or Gregorian format.

